<title>ESTONIA: NEW GOVERNMENT SWORN IN ON MARCH 17.</title>
<headline>NEW GOVERNMENT SWORN IN ON MARCH 17.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the list of the</p>
<p>new Estonian government approved by President Lennart Meri on</p>
<p>Saturday. The new prime minister and agriculture and education</p>
<p>ministers took the oath of office on Monday.</p>
<p>Changes in the list are marked with a *.</p>
<p> Prime Minister.............Mart Siimann (CP)</p>
<p>*Agriculture..............Andres VARIK (MU)</p>
<p> Culture....................Jaak ALLIK (CP)</p>
<p> Defence..................Andres OOVEL (CP)</p>
<p> Economy....................Jaak LEIMANN (non-party)</p>
<p>*Education..................Mait KLAASSEN (non-party)</p>
<p> Environment...............Villu REILJAN (MU)</p>
<p> Finance....................Mart OPMANN (CP)</p>
<p> Foreign..................Toomas ILVES (non-party)</p>
<p> Interior..................Riivo SINIJAERV (CP)</p>
<p> Justice....................Paul VARUL (CP)</p>
<p> Social Affairs.............Tiiu ARO (non-party)</p>
<p>Transport &amp; Communication.Raivo VARE (non-party)</p>
<p>JUNIOR MINISTERS (Ministers Without Portfolio):</p>
<p> European Affairs..........Andra VEIDEMANN (DP)</p>
<p>*Regional Affiars......... Unfilled</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>CP -- Coalition Party</p>
<p>DP -- Development Party</p>
<p>MU -- Rural Union</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom, + 372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
